@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Brain tumor research in plain language";
}

@* Entry Hub home per docs/design/entry-hub-handoff/index.html. The feed grid
   and digest signup arrive with M2 data and WI-107 copy; until then the hub
   is the whole page. Door targets are sitemap.md URLs (dead until their
   items land — same policy as the nav). *@
<section class="hub" aria-labelledby="hub-title">
    <h1 id="hub-title">Brain tumor research, in plain language.</h1>
    <p>
        Every day we read new brain tumor research and news, then explain it
        in words anyone can understand. A person reviews every summary before
        it is published, and we always tell you how early a finding is — and
        what it does <em>not</em> mean.
    </p>
    <div class="hub__doors">
        <a class="door door--primary" href="/start">
            <strong>Just diagnosed? Start here.</strong>
            <span class="sub">Your diagnosis words, questions to ask, and where to find support.</span>
            <span class="door__cta">Start here →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="door" href="/research">
            <strong>Browse all research</strong>
            <span class="sub">Every update, sorted by how well tested it is.</span>
            <span class="door__cta">Browse →</span>
        </a>
        <a class="door" href="/get-help-now">
            <strong>Talk to someone now</strong>
            <span class="sub">The free ABTA CareLine: 800-886-2282.</span>
            <span class="door__cta">More help →</span>
        </a>
    </div>
</section>

@* The feed and digest signup land with M2/M4 data; until then the hub and
   these honest pointers are the page. *@
<p>
    The daily research feed and the weekly digest are coming soon. In the
    meantime, you can read
    <a href="/how-we-write">how we write these summaries</a>, look up a word
    in the <a href="/glossary">glossary</a>, or read more about brain tumors
    at the
    <a href="https://www.cancer.gov/types/brain">National Cancer Institute</a>.
</p>
